{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_STEM_Simplified\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by STEM Simplified</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Mika would like to estimate how far she can ride a new model of electric bike on a fully charged battery. She completed two trips totaling <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles. The first trip used <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the total battery power, while the second trip used <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0cf2a41ca6fbaafe3d21b823a9bed30c7272fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of the total battery power. How many miles can this electric bike go on a fully charged battery?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c66f43b667ccf11fa4687982f34e94f316e1b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 45\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 48\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 50\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 52\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 55\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"434\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that the total battery spent is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a98ba03236c1739c864c3f4f096536bdd985e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{3}{10} = \\frac{5+3}{10} = \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" />. We can thus write the proportion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/117e1c20f42b03c1670acc4e758c06d2bff09d92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{\\frac{4}{5}} = \\frac{x}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"63\" height=\"45\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ebb4daea36cc5a10aafa7fcf44cd5e0ee1ef83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{\\frac{4}{5}} = 40\\cdot \\frac{5}{4} = \\boxed{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"146\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>~OlympiadMaster\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The fully charged battery has a total battery power <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. There is a bijective analysis that if one uses a set speed for both ways in a directional plane, the amount <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the farthest they can travel. Then, after the first trip, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec4b0b3f80cef66ed0100e91181040537cd3323b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> is used. Then, after the second, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c6ae41da9e775e8956ed9bc2281ffe504d1bb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{10}P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" /> is used. Thus, the total distance traveled (40 miles) corresponds to the total fraction of battery used:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/037e485b9183b97c075a9790f1311aa62711e585.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}P + \\frac{3}{10}P = 40\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"37\" />\nTo clear the denominators, we multiply by 10:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7b33e9a72d41fd6e7543e333d54da11478934bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5P + 3P = 400\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/6/bc600d63d4e512b22b76294517d50ff52e630415.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8P = 400\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92cb656f767cfc012c46ecbef536fb4b4229621.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P = 50\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />\nThe answer is clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be5ea4d09f84dc246df73b5920b249b013503fb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start with combining the battery fractions listed in the problem, and we compare that to the number of miles she rode.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f869212828b694477f61eacccc07d6559b3df9bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{3}{10} = \\frac{8}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/04733596658bf732c5e8e3c9f4db4790c8c16681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> of her battery power.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b81c6f401030f2f46b1a16298c4c07f33e9719.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{8}{10}x = 40\\]\" width=\"72\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc8b6e819a6fa6b9fb99d47d1d48b892acb0aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1950f12a711d2fa9f660bcfaa0c72da23d5981.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{10}{8} \\cdot \\frac{8}{10}x = 40 \\cdot \\frac{10}{8}\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f4c540528c4a907639809244f52365cf7a4c757.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{400}{8}\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be5ea4d09f84dc246df73b5920b249b013503fb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Ingeniouspeacock36\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_STEM_Simplified\">Video Solution by STEM Simplified</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by STEM Simplified\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zz3a8KC_jSs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zz3a8KC_jSs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/9jCyQU4sNvI\">https://youtu.be/9jCyQU4sNvI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=629s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=629s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1aLMe6zEYv/\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1aLMe6zEYv/</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\